    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the bug where `frai gate init --ci` wasn't creating the GitHub Actions workflow file. \n\n**The Problem:** \nCommander.js was parsing the `--ci` flag as a top-level option on the parent program, so it got consumed before the gate subcommand handler received the arguments. The `args` array only contained `['init']` instead of `['init', '--ci']`.\n\n**The Solution:**\nModified `/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` to reconstruct the gate command arguments directly from `process.argv` rather than relying on Commander's parsed args. This ensures all flags and options are properly passed through to the frai-gate CLI.\n\n**Changes Made:**\n- Line 753-754: Added code to find the 'gate' index in `process.argv` and slice everything after it, preserving all flags including `--ci`\n\n**Verification:**\n\u2705 Rebuilt the package with `pnpm --filter frai build`\n\u2705 Tested with `frai gate init --ci` in a clean directory\n\u2705 Both files now created correctly:\n  - `FRAI-SPEC.md`\n  - `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`",
